at smartphone has  become a prime tool of rights activists  in Pakistan  make their voice being heard over 30  activists are live-streaming the protest  and this was a protest of about a few  hundred people we talk about censorship  has anyone commented about censorship  and the fact that this movement isn't  being reported on yeah I think  unfortunately for the I think for the  large part a lot of a lot of TV channels  are not even trying to cover them  anymore but there was there is this one  TV presenter who explained why the last  segment of her TV program was dropped  earlier this week she wrote on Twitter  saying because I reported on more st.  hours arrest more scene is one of the  Parliamentarians  linked with PTM and she wrote that she  asked on what charges was he arrested  but it was censored and she wrote  welcome to censor East on where people  must suffer in silence  well up till now this state has seemed  unsure of how to deal with Monzer posh  teen he emphasizes peaceful  demonstration and upholding the  Constitution here's an excerpt from a  speech he gave last year in Lahore to  the people who call us traitors the  Constitution of Pakistan shows who is a  real traitor article 19 in Pakistan's  Constitution says that the people have  freedom of speech article 6 of  Pakistan's Constitution clearly says  anyone who sabotages the Constitution is  a traitor how many times have these  generals sabotage this Constitution shut  up  so is he correctly quoting the  Constitution there and if so do the  charges of hate speech and Sedition  against him hold any water well most  people don't think so basically he's  calling for accountability of powerful  people in the Pakistani army people who  are allegedly involved in ordering  killings and abductions and committing  torture and abuses and it says it is a  machine it has been seen before in  Pakistan at any one whether they are  politician writers journalists activists  when they call for that accountability 